ructing the agent to retry a completed close."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1457","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:57:30.561Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:57:30.561Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: full2959-item corpus includes completed historical close warning and failure recovery owners; fresh request-specific search and open/in-progress reads found no owner for success receipt identity. GH1464 body and all comments read; report observed2026.10.13. This is intake only and remains open, unclaimed. Related cursor UX work is separately active under pm-gh1457."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"11a166e8268d8041e27cef93a674db97ff9c3934c14642f9687db123a201e3d9","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"91b5d140b217817070fe347903782ec777f0dd3954548659756b95b1d73bc16f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-14T05:58:01.019Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"c55fa3824028333991367803","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1457","claim:pm-gh1458","release:pm-7zs0"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1457+pm-gh1458","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1457","claim:pm-gh1458","release:pm-7zs0"]}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1464\n\n## Problem\n\nA **successful** `pm close <id> \"<reason>\" --validate-close warn` (exit 0, `status: \"closed\"`) prints a `recovery:` block containing `suggested_retry` and `suggested_retry_args`. Every other `recovery` / `suggested_retry` an agent sees in pm output belongs to a failed command, so agents read this one as a failure too.\n\nObserved on 2026.10.13 (orchestrator session, 2026-10-14): I closed three items with warn-mode validation. Output piped through `tail -2` showed only the two `suggested_retry*` lines, so I re-ran `pm close`. The retry failed with `Item … is already terminal; use pm update …`: one wasted round trip, an error, and briefly the belief that the close had not happened.\n\n## Repro\n\n```bash\nd=$(mktemp -d) && cd \"$d\" && git init -q && pm init >/dev/null\nid=$(pm create --type Task --title \"Probe\" --description d --acceptance-criteria a --json | jq -r .item.id)\npm close \"$id\" \"done\" --validate-close warn; echo \"exit=$?\"\n```\n\nOutput (abridged):\n\n```\nstatus: \"closed\"\nwarnings[1]: \"close_validation_missing_fields:pm-6lay:resolution (--resolution),expected_result (--expected-result),actual_result (--actual-result)\"\nrecovery:\n  missing[3]: \"--resolution\",\"--expected-result\",\"--actual-result\"\n  suggested_retry: \"pm --pm-path …/.agents/pm update pm-6lay --resolution \\\"<value>\\\" --expected-result \\\"<value>\\\" --actual-result \\\"<value>\\\"\"\nexit=0\n```\n\n## Suggested change\n\n1. On success, rename the block to a non-failure key, for example `follow_up:` with `suggested_command`, so `recovery`/`retry` keep their meaning (the command failed, here is how to re-run it).\n2. Since `pm close` already accepts `--resolution`, `--expected-result` and `--actual-result`, mention them in the warning and in the generated AGENTS.md quickstart (`pm close <id> \"<evidence>\" --validate-close warn`). Agents can then close with full evidence in one call instead of close + update.\n\nRelated, all closed: #953, #757, #519 (failure-path recovery bundles for `pm close`), #1203."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-14T05:58:01.019Z"}],"before_hash":"11a166e8268d8041e27cef93a674db97ff9c3934c14642f9687db123a201e3d9","after_hash":"4e2a84f29bbb621393ccce4a1df1bc0908ba61de099acaa84315c090b5cd506b","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Preserve complete GitHub report in canonical intake","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b67f7b74a73a6cb9cf4cfa5ab846e01f2b29d8f2e4cfae79d85e67f6eaed893e"}
